 matches found: --include=*.go\nMakefile:4:.PHONY: build test lint fmt clean cve-fixtures lts-fixtures lint-scanner-fixtures chart-test image-test agent-image agent-image-test\nMakefile:31:agent-image:\nMakefile:35:# Checks ard-agent:dev (needs Docker; run `make agent-image` first; not part of `make test`).\nMakefile:36:agent-image-test:\nMakefile:37:\tdeploy/test-agent-image.sh ard-agent:dev\ndocs/proposal.md:526:- **Agent image.** The default `ard-agent` image (`deploy/agent/Dockerfile`: the `claude` CLI pinned to `claude.TestedVersion` with per-architecture checksums, git and common linters; no `gh`, no credential helper, no AGPL tools) is built locally with `make agent-image` as `ard-agent:dev` and checked with `make agent-image-test`. It is never published, to a public registry or to GHCR, and `ard-build` does not build it. `TestAgentImagePins` fails when the Dockerfile's version or checksums fall out of step with `TestedVersion`.\n// Package executor defines the contract for running one agent job somewhere\n// and reporting back. It holds plain data types only and imports nothing from\n// config, state, agent or github, so other executors (Kubernetes, Phase 3)\n// can implement the same five calls.\npackage executor\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\n// Executor runs one agent job. The controller keeps the Handle (as JSON) and\n// passes it back on every call; the executor keeps no durable state.\ntype Executor interface {\n\t// Prepare creates the workspace, writes inputs and opens log files. It\n\t// starts no process.\n\tPrepare(ctx context.Context, j Job) (Handle, error)\n\t// Start launches c without blocking. The ctx does not bound the process:\n\t// only the job deadline and Cleanup stop it.\n\tStart(ctx context.Context, h Handle, c Command) (Handle, error)\n\tStatus(ctx context.Context, h Handle) (Status, error)\n\tLogs(ctx context.Context, h Handle, o LogsOptions) (io.ReadCloser, error)\n\t// Cleanup stops the process if needed and